1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Your nutrition assistant, under your control.
Local AI. Private records. Cloud when you choose.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This is Metria. I choose a fictional food photo
and confirm cloud analysis.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
NVIDIA Nemotron returns a draft
with foods, portions, and uncertainty.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
I review it, then choose to save.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Now I ask: “How many calories
were in my latest meal?”

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Metria answers from the meal
saved on this phone.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,000
The model selects a tool. Metria reads
the local record and checks the answer.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Nutrition is calculated from food data and portions,
rather than invented by the chat model.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The assistant proposes.
The user decides what gets saved.

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Gemma assists on-device. MiniLM can route
supported local questions without invoking Gemma.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Or choose Nemotron through Nebius,
which selects tools for cloud chat.

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Cloud processes submitted content. Saved records
and tool execution stay on your phone.

13
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
For this demo, the broker
runs locally in Docker.

14
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:21,000
You enter your own Nebius API key
at a hidden prompt.

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:28,000
The app connects through a temporary HTTPS tunnel,
using a private access pass.

16
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,000
The broker keeps the provider key outside the app
and enforces request limits.

17
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
The cloud model is NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Super VL,
served by Nebius Token Factory.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
It handles the photo draft and chat decisions.
Record tools execute on the phone.

19
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Photo analysis is an estimate. Hidden ingredients
and uncertain portions still need review.

20
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The app validates model output,
and saving always requires your confirmation.

21
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Cloud mode needs internet and Nebius credits.
This demo has no permanently hosted broker.

22
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:21,000
To reproduce it, run Docker locally with your own key
and follow the setup guide.

23
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Metria brings meal review and record-grounded
answers into one workflow.
